NAME
    test_memcpy_peer - test xpu_memcpy_peer API

SYNOPSIS
    test_memcpy_peer [--unit] [--perf] [--auto] 
             [--loop <loop_count>] [-hv] <src_id> <dst_id> <size>

DESCRIPTION
    Perform the xpu_memcpy_peer test. The basic test process is DMA <size> bytes from
    XPU device src_id memory A into XPU device dst_id memory B. This whole process will
    be executed in <loop_count> interations.

OPTIONS
    --unit  Test the correntness of xpu_memcpy_peer API, the src_id dst_id size must
            provided.

    --perf  Test the performance of xpu_memcpy_peer API, the src_id dst_id size must
            provided.

    --auto  Automaticly test the performance and correctness of xpu_memcpy_peer API. The
            process is getting the current device count and forming a ring for all XPU
            devices. Then, performing xpu_memcpy_peer across the ring.

    --l3  Set test memory type to L3, default to HBM.
    --loop <loop_count>  Do <loop_count> iteration of DMA test in total, 1 if not set.

    -v  Print verbose information.

    -h  Print this message
